                            <comment id="494339" author="gerrit" created="Sun, 10 May 2026 23:05:01 +0000">&lt;p&gt;"Aboo Valappil &amp;lt;vadakkumuri.valappil.abooback@oracle.com&amp;gt;" uploaded a new patch: &lt;a href="https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/65791" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/65791&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
Subject: &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-18638" title="print project name with &amp;#39;lfs project&amp;#39;" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-18638"&gt;LU-18638&lt;/a&gt; lfs: print project names by default&lt;br/&gt;
Project: fs/lustre-release&lt;br/&gt;
Branch: master&lt;br/&gt;
Current Patch Set: 1&lt;br/&gt;
Commit: 441a876a4fcbc7a20f58bd482e4f292e6d0f6933&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="494018" author="adilger" created="Mon, 4 May 2026 19:59:20 +0000">&lt;p&gt;I was wondering about that as well, but if &lt;tt&gt;lfs project&lt;/tt&gt; is printing out the project name, then it should also accept the project name as &lt;em&gt;input&lt;/em&gt; to the various commands (&lt;tt&gt;lfs project&lt;/tt&gt;, &lt;tt&gt;lfs quota&lt;/tt&gt;, &lt;tt&gt;lfs find&lt;/tt&gt;, etc.) so I think it should be OK.  Printing out &lt;b&gt;both&lt;/b&gt; the number and the name is definitely going to cause problems.  Also, it will only print the name if &lt;tt&gt;/etc/projid&lt;/tt&gt; contains the &lt;tt&gt;name:number&lt;/tt&gt; mapping, which will not be true for most systems, so the transition will be gradual and under the control of the sysadmin.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="494016" author="JIRAUSER19323" created="Mon, 4 May 2026 19:12:58 +0000">&lt;p&gt;@andrews Dilger - I pushed a PR but, it requires some rework. &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul class="alternate" type="square"&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;It currently prints both id and name. This will be hanged. However, when this is changed, I am wondering if there is a worry that existing tools that depends on the "lfs project" might get a different behavior printing the name instead of id. This might cause some sort of regression in those tools? &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
</comment>
                            <comment id="494015" author="gerrit" created="Mon, 4 May 2026 19:07:11 +0000">&lt;p&gt;"Aboo Valappil &amp;lt;vadakkumuri.valappil.abooback@oracle.com&amp;gt;" uploaded a new patch: &lt;a href="https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/65664" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/65664&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
Subject: &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-18638" title="print project name with &amp;#39;lfs project&amp;#39;" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-18638"&gt;LU-18638&lt;/a&gt; utils: print project name with 'lfs project'&lt;br/&gt;
