                            <comment id="493933" author="adilger" created="Sat, 2 May 2026 20:28:48 +0000">&lt;p&gt;Lu-12480 is for adding a &lt;tt&gt;STATX_PROJID&lt;/tt&gt; extension to the &lt;tt&gt;statx()&lt;/tt&gt; syscall in the Linux kernel to fetch the PROJID along with other inode attributes, instead of having to fetch it separately. &lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="493932" author="adilger" created="Sat, 2 May 2026 20:26:43 +0000">&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20207" title="llapi_project_get() should cache /etc/projid contents for repeated lookups" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-20207"&gt;LU-20207&lt;/a&gt; is for implementing an in-memory cache for &lt;tt&gt;/etc/projid&lt;/tt&gt; lookups. &lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="493931" author="JIRAUSER19323" created="Sat, 2 May 2026 19:10:32 +0000">&lt;p&gt;I am working on this and ready with a PR. Just waiting to be able to push a PR to the review. &lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="441254" author="adilger" created="Wed, 15 Jan 2025 18:58:34 +0000">&lt;p&gt;For commands like "ls" they will default to printing the name, if it can be looked up, and print the number of the lookup fails.  "ls -n" will only print the number, for cases where that is important, or if the name lookup is slow/broken (eg. using a network LDAP database that is overloaded or offline).&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I &lt;em&gt;think&lt;/em&gt; "lfs quota" is doing the same (prefer name, fall back to number).&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
